@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line here
   ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error: an unbound tag helper survives
   into the response as its own start tag rather than throwing. The <page-header> tag helper in
   SyncAudit.cshtml needs the @addTagHelper line, not just the @using. Guarded by
   MonitorPageRenderTests (Humans.Integration.Tests — local-only, CI filters it out).

   No @inject IStringLocalizer line: the section carries no resource set at all. Its one page
   is admin-only English. Nothing pins that — it is documentation, not an assertion. *@
@using Humans.Base.Extensions
@using Humans.Monitor
@using Humans.Monitor.Models
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Models
@using Humans.Base.ViewComponents
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
@* <vc:google-sync-log> (Monitor/SyncAudit) is the GoogleIntegration section's own component;
   without this line the element ships as inert literal markup with a green build. *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.GoogleIntegration
